.TH IAD\-AS\-BUTTON 3 "" "iced-adaptive-design 0.1.0" "iced-adaptive-design Manual"
.SH NAME
as_button \- Makes any content a button: as_button(ItemRow::new(..)).on_press(m)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
as_button(content: impl Into<Element<'a, M>>)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Makes any content a button: \fBas_button(ItemRow::new(..)).on_press(m)\fR. A button is events, not layout: no padding, no width of its own, no surface. The content keeps its size and its look (a card draws its own surface), and the button adds the press and a hover/press tint over exactly its bounds. \fB.style(..)\fR swaps the tint, e.g. \fBflat_row\fR.
